    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-d/q1-question-1.svg\" alt=\"In a histogram the weights of peaches, correct to the nearest gram, are plotted on the x axis. In this histogram the class 146 150 − has a frequency of 75 and is represented by a rectangle of base 2.8 cm and height 7.5 cm. In the same histogram a different class is represented by a rectangle of base 5.6 cm and height 10.5 cm. Determine the frequency of this class. ( ) 4\" style=\"--madas-width:577.3px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-d/q1-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"The first interval has width 150.5 −145.5 = 5 [B1] and frequency 75, hence density 75/5 = 15.\" style=\"--madas-width:608.0px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-d/q1-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"Let the corresponding width and density for the second rectangle be x and y. [A1] From the horizontal and vertical scales, 2.8 = x 5 7.5 15 = 10.5 =⇒ x = 10, =⇒ y = 21. [A1] 5.6 y Cross-multiplication gives 2.8x = 28 and 7.5y = 157.5. Its frequency is width times density, 10(21) = 210 . [A1] Alternative working. Histogram area is proportional to frequency. The area of the second rectangle is 5.6(10.5), while 2.8(7.5) corresponds to 75 peaches: The areas are 58.8 cm2 and 21 cm2 respectively, a scale factor 58.8/21 = 2.8. The frequency is 755.6(10.5) 2.8(7.5) = 210 .\" style=\"--madas-width:678.7px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 1 is 4 marks.</p>"
    ],
    "promptText": "In a histogram the weights of peaches, correct to the nearest gram, are plotted on the x axis. In this histogram the class 146 150 − has a frequency of 75 and is represented by a rectangle of base 2.8 cm and height 7.5 cm. In the same histogram a different class is represented by a rectangle of base 5.6 cm and height 10.5 cm. Determine the frequency of this class. ( ) 4"
  },
