    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-d/q4-question-1.svg\" alt=\"The ages of the residents of Arnold Street are denoted by x the ages of the residents of Benedict Street are denoted by y . These are summarized in the following back to back stem and leaf diagram. x y 5 0 5,5,3,3 1 9,9,1 2 5 9,8,6,5,5,4,3,2,2,2,1 3 6,7,8 6,4,1,0,0,0,0 4 1,2,2,3,4,8 9 5 1,4,4,4,4,5,8,8 6 1,3,4,4,5,9,9 7 2,6,9\" style=\"--madas-width:558.7px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-d/q4-question-2.svg\" alt=\"where 2 3 9 = 32 in Arnold Street and 39 in Benedict Street . a) Find separately for the residents of Arnold Street and Benedict Street, ... i. ... the mode. ii. ... the lower quartile, the median and the upper quartile. ( 10 ) iii. ... the mean and the standard deviation.     2 2 You may assume x = 866 , x = 31514 , y = 1516 , y = 86880 . A coefficient of skewness is defined as mean − mode\" style=\"--madas-width:577.3px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-d/q4-question-3.svg\" alt=\". standard deviation ( ) b) Evaluate this coefficient for the ages in each street. 1 c) Compare the distribution of the ages between the two streets. ( ) 3\" style=\"--madas-width:574.7px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-d/q4-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"(a) Read these back-to-back leaves using a common tens stem: For example 2 | 3 | 9 means ages 32 and 39 on the left and right respectively: Arnold Stem Benedict 5 0 5 5 3 3 1 9 9 1 2 5 9 8 6 5 5 4 3 2 2 2 1 3 6 7 8 6 4 1 0 0 0 0 4 1 2 2 3 4 8 9 5 1 4 4 4 4 5 8 8 6 1 3 4 4 5 9 9 7 2 6 9 The stem-and-leaf diagram contains 27 ages for Arnold Street and 28 for Benedict Street: [B1] [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:673.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-d/q4-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"(i) The most frequent ages are 40 in Arnold Street and 54 in Benedict Street: [M1] [A1] (ii) For Arnold Street, use (27 + 1)/4 = 7, (27 + 1)/2 = 14, 3(27 + 1)/4 = 21, so take observations 7, 14 and 21. [M1] For Benedict Street, average observations 7 and 8 for Q1, 14 and 15 for the median, and 21 and 22 for Q3 . [A1] (iii) Using the supplied sums, calculate the means and population standard deviations: ¯x = 866 r31514 −¯x2 ≈11.77, 27 ≈32.07, σx = 27 r86880 ¯y = 1516 −¯y2 ≈13.09. ≈54.14, σy = 28 28 [B1] [A1] Street Mode Q1 Median Q3 Mean Standard deviation Arnold 40 29 34 40 32.07 11.77 Benedict 54 42.5 54 64 54.14 13.09\" style=\"--madas-width:680.0px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-d/q4-solution-3.svg\" alt=\"[M1] [A1] (b) The coefficients are (32.07 −40)/11.77 ≈−0.67 and (54.14 −54)/13.09 ≈0.01 , respectively: [A1] (c) Benedict Street has higher mean and median ages: [B1] For comparison, the interquartile ranges are 40 −29 = 11 and 64 −42.5 = 21.5. Its standard deviation and interquartile range are larger: [A1] Arnold Street shows negative skew, whereas Benedict Street is close to symmetric according to the coefficient. [A1] Source note. The Arnold Street leaves give sums 867 and 31539. The calculation uses the supplied values of 866 and 31514, as in the handwritten working.\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 4 is 14 marks.</p>"
    ],
    "promptText": "The ages of the residents of Arnold Street are denoted by x the ages of the residents of Benedict Street are denoted by y . These are summarized in the following back to back stem and leaf diagram. x y 5 0 5,5,3,3 1 9,9,1 2 5 9,8,6,5,5,4,3,2,2,2,1 3 6,7,8 6,4,1,0,0,0,0 4 1,2,2,3,4,8 9 5 1,4,4,4,4,5,8,8 6 1,3,4,4,5,9,9 7 2,6,9 where 2 3 9 = 32 in Arnold Street and 39 in Benedict Street . a) Find separately for the residents of Arnold Street and Benedict Street, ... i. ... the mode. ii. ... the lower quartile, the median and the upper quartile. ( 10 ) iii. ... the mean and the standard deviation.     2 2 You may assume x = 866 , x = 31514 , y = 1516 , y = 86880 . A coefficient of skewness is defined as mean − mode . standard deviation ( ) b) Evaluate this coefficient for the ages in each street. 1 c) Compare the distribution of the ages between the two streets. ( ) 3"
