    "id": "madas/alevel-applied-d/q7",
    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-d/q7-question-1.svg\" alt=\"The discrete random variable X has the following probability distribution x 1 3 0 1 1 1 P X ( = x ) 6 3 2 Three independent observations of X are made, denoted by X , X and X . 1 2 3 Calculate ( ) P X + X + X ≥ 4 . ( ) 7 1 2 3\" style=\"--madas-width:576.0px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-d/q7-question-2.svg\" alt=\"Question diagram\" style=\"--madas-width:577.3px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-d/q7-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"The source lists the successful triples: Here are the orderings and products in full: entries sum orderings probability 0, 1, 3 4 6 6(1/6)(1/3)(1/2) = 1/6 3(1/3)2(1/2) = 1/6 1, 1, 3 5 3 3(1/3)(1/2)2 = 1/4 1, 3, 3 7 3 3(1/6)(1/2)2 = 1/8 0, 3, 3 6 3 (1/2)3 = 1/8 3, 3, 3 9 1 Adding gives 1/6 + 1/6 + 1/4 + 1/8 + 1/8 = 5/6. Source correction. The scan gives 5/8. The three distinct values in the first row have six permutations, and the 1, 1, 3 row requires the probability of 1 twice: As a check, work with the complementary event X1 + X2 + X3 ≤3. [B1] [A1] If no observation is 3, all three are 0 or 1, and the probability is (1 6 + 1 3)3 = 1 8. [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:678.7px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-d/q7-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"If a 3 occurs, both other observations must be 0. [A1] The three possible positions of the 3 contribute 3(1 2)(1 6)2 = 1 24. [A1] Therefore P(X1 + X2 + X3 ≥4) = 1 −1 8 −1 24 [M1] [A1] = 5 6 .\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 7 is 7 marks.</p>"
    ],
    "promptText": "The discrete random variable X has the following probability distribution x 1 3 0 1 1 1 P X ( = x ) 6 3 2 Three independent observations of X are made, denoted by X , X and X . 1 2 3 Calculate ( ) P X + X + X ≥ 4 . ( ) 7 1 2 3 "
