    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-d/q10-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"Fill in a speed–time graph from the information given:\" style=\"--madas-width:554.7px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-d/q10-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"(a) The gradient of the first straight segment is a = ∆v/∆t, giving 0.36 = 1.62/T. The initial accelerating phase lasts 1.62/0.36 = 4.5 s. [B1] The next boundaries occur at 19.5 and 26 seconds: [A1] (b) Alternatively, treat the whole speed graph as one trapezium with parallel sides 15 and 4.5 + 15 + 6.5 = 26 seconds: Its area is 1 2(26 + 15)(1.62) = 33.21. The area under the graph is 1.62(4.5/2 + 15 + 6.5/2) = 33.21 m . [A1] First triangular area [A1] rectangular area [A1] final triangular area [A1] sum as a distance\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-d/q10-solution-3.svg\" alt=\"(c) The normal reaction satisfies R −80g = 80a, taking upwards as positive: [M1] The largest upward acceleration is 0.36 m s−2 in the first phase: Thus R −80g = 80(0.36) . = 28.8 Hence R = 80(9.8 + 0.36) = 812.8 N . [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 10 is 8 marks.</p>"
