    "id": "madas/alevel-applied-d/q11",
    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-d/q11-question-1.svg\" alt=\"Relative to a fixed origin O , the horizontal unit vectors i and j are pointing due east and due north, respectively. 1 1 A particle P is moving with constant acceleration of ( ) ms−. 2 10 − i j 5 15 It is initially observed passing through the point with position vector ( − 20 i − j m ) 2 with velocity of ( ) ms−. 1 4 i + 2 j a) Find an expression for the position vector of P , t s after it was first observed. ( ) 2 b) Calculate the times when P is due east of the origin O . ( ) 4\" style=\"--madas-width:569.3px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-d/q11-question-2.svg\" alt=\"c) Determine the speed of  P when it is travelling in a south-eastern direction. ( ) 6\" style=\"--madas-width:569.3px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-d/q11-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"(a) Substitute the given vectors to form (−20i −15 2 j) + (4i + 2j)t + 1 2( 1 10i −1 5j)t2. Collect the coefficients of i, j. Use r = r0 + ut + 1 2at2: [M1] −20 + 4t + t2 ! 2 + 2t −t2 ! −15 r = i + j . [A1] 20 10\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-d/q11-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"(b) Due east requires a zero north component and a positive east component: Thus −15/2 + 2t −t2/10 = 0, or −75 + 20t −t2 = 0. Setting the north component to zero gives t2 −20t + 75 = 0, [M1] or (t −5)(t −15) = 0, with roots 5 and 15. [A1] The east components at these times are 1.25 and 51.25 metres, respectively: [A1] Hence both qualify: 5 s, 15 s . [A1] (c) Use v = u + at = (4i + 2j) + (i/10 −j/5)t. The velocity is (4 + t/10)i + (2 −t/5)j. [B1] For south-east, the east component is positive and is the negative of the north component: [A1] Thus 4 + t/10 = −(2 −t/5), [A1] hence 6 = t/10, giving t = 60 s. [A1] The velocity is 10i −10j, so its magnitude is √ q 102 + (−10)2 = 200 ≈14.14.\" style=\"--madas-width:678.7px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-d/q11-solution-3.svg\" alt=\"Thus the speed is √ 2 m s−1 . 10 [M1] [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 11 is 12 marks.</p>"
