      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-d/q13-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"Multiplying by 4.9 gives 294 = 1296 cos β sin β . = 648 sin 2β Therefore sin 2β = 60g/362 ≈0.45370, [A1] so 2β ≈26.98◦or 180◦−26.98◦= 153.02◦for the physical launch angles, giving β ≈13.49◦or 76.51◦. [M1] [A1] (b) The source substitutes the smaller angle into the vertical flight-time formula, giving t = 36 sin(13.49◦)/4.9 = 1.71 . . . s. The smaller angle gives the larger horizontal speed and the shorter time: [M1] Thus 60 t = 36 cos 13.49◦≈1.71 s . [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:678.7px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 13 is 10 marks.</p>"
