      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-d/q14-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"(a) Taking moments about A √ Taking moments about A, 2aT sin θ = a mg. [M1] Cancelling a gives mg = 2T/ 5. Thus √ 5 T = 2 mg . [M1] [A1] (b) Horizontal balance gives H = T cos θ √ √ . [B1] [A1] = ( 5mg/2)(2/ 5) = mg Vertical balance gives V = mg −T sin θ √ √ . [A1] = mg −( 5mg/2)(1/ 5) = mg/2\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-d/q14-solution-3.svg\" alt=\"The resulting hinge reaction has magnitude q p H2 + V 2 = mg 1 + 1 4 √ 5 [M1] [A1] = 2 mg = T. Alternative. Since mg = 2T sin θ, the vertical component is also T sin θ. Hence H2 + V 2 = T 2 cos2 θ + T 2 sin2 θ = T 2, and the reaction magnitude is T.\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
